        modelAnswer: "(a) In Tamil Nadu, approximately 94% of all Fair Price Shops are managed by cooperative societies.\n\n(b) Amul's White Revolution:\nAmul established an organized network of rural dairy cooperative societies in Anand (Gujarat), pooling milk directly from millions of small and marginal farmers. By eliminating exploitative middlemen, setting up modern pasteurization and cold-storage processing plants, and distributing dairy products nationwide, Amul drastically increased national milk production (Operation Flood) and ensured fair, guaranteed incomes to rural households.\n\n(c) Initiative in Delhi:\nMother Dairy (established under Operation Flood by the National Dairy Development Board), which provides quality milk and fresh vegetables (under the \"Safal\" brand) at controlled, subsidized prices through thousands of community booths across Delhi-NCR.",
